From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hotty Agent <hotty@neuroplast.io>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 01:41:42 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 47/47] hottyterm: a key's replies reach the program before its
 echo is painted

A key for the surface holding the keyboard went to hotty-blitz, then the
surface painted its echo, inline under the terminal's lock, and only then
did `deliver` queue the key's replies (the keys the surface didn't use and
the events it heard) for the pty. A program that answers the key, such as
plx's palette filtering its list, began only once the echo was painted.

`keyPressed` and `keyBytes` now send the replies to the IO thread's
mailbox, and wake it, before they paint. The order of the replies is
kept; what the paint finds for the program (`fit`, `caret`) follows them
in `deliver`, as before.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/termio/hotty.zig | 18 ++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 18 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/termio/hotty.zig b/src/termio/hotty.zig
index 4723b9c44..69944a158 100644
--- a/src/termio/hotty.zig
+++ b/src/termio/hotty.zig
@@ -1200,6 +1200,22 @@ pub const Hotty = struct {
         handler.termio_messaged = true;
     }
 
+    /// A key's replies, sent before its echo is painted (gov R-22): a
+    /// program that answers the key, such as plx's palette, then works while
+    /// the surface paints instead of after it. They keep their order, and
+    /// what the paint finds for the program (`fit`, `caret`) follows them.
+    /// The callers hold the lock, which a full mailbox's send lets go
+    /// meanwhile, as `osc`'s does; none runs read-only.
+    fn sendKeyReplies(self: *Hotty) void {
+        if (self.replies.items.len == 0) return;
+        const handler = self.streamHandler();
+        // Out of memory: `deliver` tries again after the paint.
+        const msg = termio.Message.writeReq(self.alloc, self.replies.items) catch return;
+        self.replies.clearRetainingCapacity();
+        handler.termio_mailbox.send(msg, handler.renderer_state.mutex);
+        handler.termio_mailbox.notify();
+    }
+
     /// Termio.threadEnter: the IO thread's loop, for the timer and the
     /// wakeup.
     pub fn threadEnter(self: *Hotty, loop: *xev.Loop) void {
@@ -2164,6 +2180,7 @@ pub const Hotty = struct {
         const h = self.hostReady() orelse return false;
         const fx = self.effects();
         const consumed = hotty_host_key_pressed(h, namePtr(p.physical), p.physical.len, namePtr(p.character), p.character.len, &fx);
+        self.sendKeyReplies();
         if (self.render(t)) self.drew = true;
         // A key that scrolled shows scrollbars, which fade.
         self.schedule(t);
@@ -2178,6 +2195,7 @@ pub const Hotty = struct {
         if (bytes.len == 0) return false;
         const fx = self.effects();
         const consumed = hotty_host_key_bytes(h, bytes.ptr, bytes.len, &fx);
+        self.sendKeyReplies();
         if (self.render(t)) self.drew = true;
         // A key that scrolled shows scrollbars, which fade.
         self.schedule(t);
